  "chapter": {
    "number": 8,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "For the end, concerning the wine presses, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, our Lord, how wonderful is your name in all the earth! for your magnificence is exalted above the heavens.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings have you perfected praise, because of your enemies; that you might put down the enemy and avenger.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I will regard the heavens, the work of your fingers; the moon and stars, which you have established.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What is man, that you are mindful of him? or the son of man, that you visit him?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You made him a little less than angels, you have crowned him with glory and honor;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and you have set him over the works of your hands: you have put all things under his feet:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "sheep and all",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 15
          },
          {
            "text": "oxen, yes and the cattle of the field;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "the birds of the sky, and the fish of the sea, the creatures passing through the paths of the sea.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord our Lord, how wonderful is your name in all the earth!",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
